2026-10-27  Mentat (for Corwin; claude-sonnet-5-5, directed and checked by claude-mythos-5-1)  <corwin@bru.st>

	TopoForge 1.7: a page on the same origin can open a drawing with
	?load=<path> (a CSV or TopoForge JSON); any other origin, and file://,
	is refused and said; window.TopoForge.importCSV for the kit.  From
	h/PATCH-2026-10-27-topoforge-load-same-origin.md, with the changes to
	it listed under index.html below.
	* index.html (TF_VERSION): 1.7.  (header comment): The 1.7 line and
	who made ?load=.
	(loadFromQuery): New; boot() calls it last.  Reads ?load=, resolves it
	against the page, refuses file: and any other origin with a toast
	before any request is made, then fetches with same-origin
	credentials.  A body whose first header cell is name or hostname goes
	to importCSV; anything else to normalizeDoc as TopoForge JSON.  A bad
	status says "load failed: 404 Not Found" and the like.
	(boot): The sample drawing is not loaded on a first visit when ?load=
	names something.  Without this a first visit showed the sample with
	the rows added to it: 23 nodes for a 4-row CSV.
	Changes to the patch as proposed: toasts use 'error', since the page
	has no 'warn' style; a CSV load does not add a "Loaded" toast, since
	importCSV already says "Imported N devices" or its own error, and the
	extra toast would say Loaded after a failure; importCSV was already in
	window.TopoForge in 1.6, so it is not listed twice; the sample guard
	is new.
	* tests/browser/topoforge.browser.mjs: New checks "load 1" to "load 5"
	(the five the patch owes) and "load 1b" (a JSON drawing opens) and
	"load 1c" (without ?load= a first visit still shows the sample).  They
	serve index.html from a throwaway server on 127.0.0.1, with a second
	server on another port as the other origin (it allows any origin and
	holds a good CSV, so only the page's own test can refuse it; the
	checks also require it was never asked).  New --load-only mode: those
	checks alone, no axe-core, written to RESULT-load.txt (first line
	PARTIAL-GREEN or PARTIAL-RED), never to RESULT.txt.
	* tests/browser/prove-red.sh: New.  Plants a fault in a copy of
	index.html (the origin test, the sample guard, the file: test) and
	requires exactly the check that watches it to go red; a control run
	on the unplanted file must be green first.  All three are caught.
	* tests/browser/RESULT.txt: Rewritten by the full kit against the 1.7
	index.html where axe-core is (Chromium 153, Playwright 1.63, axe-core
	4.14): GREEN, 41 of 41 checks, no axe finding of any level, with
	Bryant's 1.5 beside it.  RESULT-load.txt, which --load-only writes,
	is a local note and is not shipped.
	* README.org, NEWS, RECIPE.org: The 1.7 line; how to run --load-only
	and prove-red.sh; the Files table and the ingredients row say 1.7.
	* patches/topoforge-1.6-to-1.7.patch: New.  v1.6 to v1.7 as one diff -u
	over the files above that changed, index.html first (not RESULT.txt
	or SHA256SUMS, which the kit and bin/sums.sh write).
	* SHA256SUMS: Regenerated with bin/sums.sh over the whole tree.

