2026-10-08  Mentat (for Corwin; claude-opus-5-5), builder T1  <corwin@bru.st>

	TopoForge 1.6: the drawing tells its own story.
	* index.html (ensureRefs): New.  Every shape and connector gets a
	lasting handle, data.tf_ref, the moment it exists; broken, missing or
	repeated handles are replaced, and the first holder on a page keeps
	its handle.
	(reindex): Calls ensureRefs, so the stamp rides the user's own edit
	and adds no undo step.
	(factsOf, parseFact): New.  The drawing as FACTS v=1 lines (pure).
	(storyOf, changesOf): New.  Plain sentences built only from the
	facts, each citing its shapes' handles; a Gaps section by fixed rules;
	what changed between two sets of facts.
	(storyMarkdown, mdSentence, htmlParts): New.  The story as Markdown:
	one facts block in a fresh fence, user words quoted and escaped, a
	header naming the drawing JSON and the facts by sha256.
	(sha256hex, sha256hexSync): New.  crypto.subtle, with a built-in
	SHA-256 when it is missing (file://).
	(storySkeleton, buildStory, storySentenceHTML, scheduleStory,
	selectRef): New.  The Story tab: live, a text alternative for the
	drawing, "Recent changes" and a polite status line that says what
	changed; ref buttons select their shape; Download story (.md) saves
	the .json and the -story.md together.  Also File > Export > Story in
	words (.md).
	Inspector tabs follow the WAI-ARIA tabs pattern (roving tabindex,
	arrow keys, Home, End); Space, Enter and the arrows on side-panel
	buttons no longer reach the canvas shortcuts; focus rings show.
	SPDX lines at the top; About says 1.6 and credits both authors;
	draw.io agent says 1.6.
	* spec/FACTS-v1.md: New.  The facts grammar in plain words.
	* tests/: New.  The story's kit in POSIX sh and jq (check.sh,
	run.sh, prove-red.sh with 14 planted faults, canon.jq, facts.jq,
	tables.json, expect/), fixtures, and node harnesses that only produce
	exports (harness/).
	* patches/topoforge-1.5-to-1.6.patch: New.  v1.5 to v1.6 as one
	diff -u.

